{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "def greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the greatest common divisor of two integers a and b.\n    It uses the Euclidean algorithm and handles negative inputs by taking their absolute values.\"\"\"\n    a_abs = abs(a)\n    b_abs = abs(b)\n    while b_abs:\n        a_abs, b_abs = b_abs, a_abs % b_abs\n    return a_abs"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/11", "solution": "def string_xor(a: str, b: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Input are two strings a and b consisting only of 1s and 0s.\n    Perform binary XOR on these inputs and return result also as a string.\n    >>> string_xor('010', '110')\n    '100'\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_binary_string(a)\n    _validate_binary_string(b)\n    _validate_same_length(a, b)\n\n    result_list = []\n    for i in range(len(a)):\n        bit_a = int(a[i])\n        bit_b = int(b[i])\n        xor_result = bit_a ^ bit_b\n        result_list.append(str(xor_result))\n    return \"\".join(result_list)"}
