{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    For a given number n, finds the largest number that divides n evenly and is smaller than n.\n    Returns 1 if n is 1, a prime number, or non-positive.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The integer for which to find the largest proper divisor.\n\n    Returns:\n        The largest proper divisor of n.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> largest_divisor(15)\n        5\n        >>> largest_divisor(7)\n        1\n        >>> largest_divisor(1)\n        1\n        >>> largest_divisor(4)\n        2\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Iterate from n // 2 down to 1.\n    for i in range(n // 2, 0, -1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return i\n\n    # If no proper divisor is found (n is prime), return 1.\n    return 1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Returns a list of prime factors for a given integer `n`.\n    Factors are sorted in ascending order and include multiplicity.\"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    divisor = 2\n\n    # Use a temporary variable to modify without altering original n\n    temp_n = n\n\n    while divisor * divisor <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % divisor == 0:\n            factors.append(divisor)\n            temp_n //= divisor\n        divisor += 1\n\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n\n    return factors"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of prime factors for a given integer n,\n    ordered from smallest to largest, with each factor repeated as necessary.\"\"\"\n\n    factors: List[int] = []\n    d = 2\n    current_n = n\n\n    while d * d <= current_n:\n        while current_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            current_n //= d\n        d += 1\n\n    if current_n > 1:\n        factors.append(current_n)\n\n    return factors"}
