{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_third([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_third([5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2])\n    [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n    \"\"\"\n\n    result_list = list(l)\n\n    elements_to_sort = []\n    indices_to_replace = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            elements_to_sort.append(l[i])\n            indices_to_replace.append(i)\n\n    elements_to_sort.sort()\n\n    for i, sorted_val in zip(indices_to_replace, elements_to_sort):\n        result_list[i] = sorted_val\n\n    return result_list"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    l_prime = list(l)\n\n    # Identify elements at indices divisible by three and their original indices.\n    values_to_sort = []\n    third_indices = []\n    for i, item in enumerate(l):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            values_to_sort.append(item)\n            third_indices.append(i)\n\n    # Sort these identified elements.\n    values_to_sort.sort()\n\n    # Place the sorted elements back into l' at their original indices.\n    for i, sorted_val in zip(third_indices, values_to_sort):\n        l_prime[i] = sorted_val\n\n    return l_prime"}
