{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\nDEFAULT_DECODE_SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            start = ord('a')\n            shifted_ord = (ord(char) - start - DEFAULT_DECODE_SHIFT_AMOUNT) % ALPHABET_SIZE + start\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            start = ord('A')\n            shifted_ord = (ord(char) - start - DEFAULT_DECODE_SHIFT_AMOUNT) % ALPHABET_SIZE + start\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        else:\n            decoded_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\n\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            # Convert character to its 0-indexed position (0 for 'a', 25 for 'z').\n            original_pos = ord(char) - ord('a')\n            # Shift backward by the defined amount and handle wrap-around using modulo.\n            shifted_pos = (original_pos - SHIFT_AMOUNT) % ALPHABET_SIZE\n            # Convert the new 0-indexed position back to a lowercase character.\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_pos + ord('a')))\n        else:\n            # Non-lowercase characters are appended unchanged to the output.\n            decoded_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
