{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "import math\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the closest integer to a number string, rounding away from zero for equidistant values.\n    For example, \"14.5\" rounds to 15, and \"-14.5\" rounds to -15.\n    \"\"\"\n    number = float(value)\n\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    floor_val = math.floor(number)\n    ceil_val = math.ceil(number)\n\n    # Determine which integer is closer.\n    dist_to_floor = abs(number - floor_val)\n    dist_to_ceil = abs(number - ceil_val)\n\n    if dist_to_floor < dist_to_ceil:\n        return int(floor_val)\n    elif dist_to_ceil < dist_to_floor:\n        return int(ceil_val)\n    else: # Equidistant values (e.g., X.5), round away from zero.\n        if number > 0:\n            return int(ceil_val)\n        else: # number < 0\n            return int(floor_val)"}
