{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "def closest_integer(value: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the closest integer to a string-represented number.\n    Equidistant numbers (X.5) are rounded away from zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_float = float(value)\n\n    # Manually calculate floor and ceil without the math module.\n    # int() truncates towards zero. Adjust for negative numbers for floor, positive for ceil.\n    floor_val = int(num_float)\n    if num_float < 0 and num_float != floor_val:\n        floor_val -= 1\n\n    ceil_val = int(num_float)\n    if num_float > 0 and num_float != ceil_val:\n        ceil_val += 1\n\n    # Apply the \"round away from zero\" rule for equidistant cases (X.5).\n    if num_float - floor_val == 0.5:\n        if num_float >= 0:\n            return ceil_val  # Positive X.5 rounds up (away from zero)\n        else:\n            return floor_val # Negative X.5 rounds down (away from zero)\n    else:\n        # For other fractional parts, round to the nearest integer.\n        if abs(num_float - floor_val) < abs(num_float - ceil_val):\n            return floor_val\n        else:\n            return ceil_val"}
